IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp1-nouns`
IMPORT `cp1-div-b-contribution-rates`

-- Tests of cp1-div-b-contribution-rates.l4: sections 11.1 and 11.2.
-- Expected values are read from the text of section 11.1(1): 1.8% for employees and employers and 3.6% for self-employed
-- persons for the years 1966 to 1986. The figures put in for Schedules 1 and 2 are test inputs (the Schedules belong
-- to piece cp6), chosen only to show that the rule returns what the Schedule sets.

§ `Tests -- section 11.1`

-- 11.1(1): 1966 to 1986, both ends included.
#ASSERT `s 11.1(1) — the contribution rate for the years 1966 to 1986` `contributing as an employee` 1966 EQUALS JUST 0.018
#ASSERT `s 11.1(1) — the contribution rate for the years 1966 to 1986` `contributing as an employee` 1986 EQUALS JUST 0.018
#ASSERT `s 11.1(1) — the contribution rate for the years 1966 to 1986` `contributing as an employer` 1975 EQUALS JUST 0.018
#ASSERT `s 11.1(1) — the contribution rate for the years 1966 to 1986` `contributing as a self-employed person` 1966 EQUALS JUST 0.036
#ASSERT `s 11.1(1) — the contribution rate for the years 1966 to 1986` `contributing as a self-employed person` 1986 EQUALS JUST 0.036
#ASSERT `s 11.1(1) — the contribution rate for the years 1966 to 1986` `contributing as an employee` 1965 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11.1(1) — the contribution rate for the years 1966 to 1986` `contributing as an employee` 1987 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 11.1(2): from 1987 the Schedule 1 figure.
#ASSERT `s 11.1(2) — the contribution rate for 1987 and subsequent years` 1987 (1.9%) EQUALS JUST 0.019
#ASSERT `s 11.1(2) — the contribution rate for 1987 and subsequent years` 2024 (4.95%) EQUALS JUST 0.0495
#ASSERT `s 11.1(2) — the contribution rate for 1987 and subsequent years` 1986 (1.9%) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the whole section: the text gives nothing before 1966.
#ASSERT `s 11.1 — the contribution rate for a capacity and a year` `contributing as an employee` 1965 (9%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11.1 — the contribution rate for a capacity and a year` `contributing as an employee` 1966 (9%) EQUALS JUST 0.018
#ASSERT `s 11.1 — the contribution rate for a capacity and a year` `contributing as a self-employed person` 1986 (9%) EQUALS JUST 0.036
#ASSERT `s 11.1 — the contribution rate for a capacity and a year` `contributing as an employee` 1987 (9%) EQUALS JUST 0.09
#ASSERT `s 11.1 — the contribution rate for a capacity and a year` `contributing as an employer` 2030 (5.95%) EQUALS JUST 0.0595

§ `Tests -- section 11.2`

-- 11.2: the first and second additional rates for 2019 and subsequent years, from Schedule 2; the base tier is not touched.
#ASSERT `s 11.2 — the first or second additional contribution rate for a tier and a year` `the first additional tier` 2019 (0.5%) EQUALS JUST 0.005
#ASSERT `s 11.2 — the first or second additional contribution rate for a tier and a year` `the first additional tier` 2018 (0.5%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11.2 — the first or second additional contribution rate for a tier and a year` `the second additional tier` 2024 (4%) EQUALS JUST 0.04
#ASSERT `s 11.2 — the first or second additional contribution rate for a tier and a year` `the second additional tier` 2018 (4%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11.2 — the first or second additional contribution rate for a tier and a year` `the base tier` 2024 (4.95%) EQUALS NOTHING
